    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="806c4c74-203f-5b3d-ae26-f7efb86e9f44" activityNameId="e32345a2-1eda-58dc-bc2e-9eac575290c3" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xx Biogas, from whey, digestion, at storage</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xx Biogas, from whey, digestion, at storage
The yearly production of whey is  2800 m3. The fermentation of this amount results in a yearly biogas production of 122550 m3. Thus, 22.8 kg whey are required for the production of 1 m3 biogas. Whey digestion fulfils only one functions: production of biogas. ;
UUID: 0dc256dd-5a79-3ddc-87f6-a33b4ce283cd
Data represents the environmental exchanges due to the digestion of whey.   Emissions due to gas purification and the use of the gas for co-generation are not included. Digested matter is treated in a wastewater treatment plant.
Location: Data represents conditions in Switzerland
Technology: no information available
Time period: undefined
Production volume: 122550 m3 biogas per year
Sampling: Literature data 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_0dc256dd-5a79-3ddc-87f6-a33b4ce283cd.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
